✴️ Day 2 of 90 - Today i learned how linux actually works, what is kernel, shell basically i learn about linux architecture & some basic linux commands.

Linux - Linux is OS & everything in linux is process. It's start with systemd (PDI1)

Linux architecure : 
Hardware --- Kernel --- shell --- Application

Kernel - Kernal is a heart of linux system. It manage low level task including memory managnment, process scheduling & device drivers.
Shell - The interface between the user & the kernel. The shell interprets GUI (Graphical user interface) intraction & translate them into kernel commands.
Application -  The Programs the user runs daily such as web browser, Text editor etc ...

Some basic commands that i practice today.

- pwd - Present Working Directory
- cd - change working directory
- ls - List available file & folders
- cat - Read file 
- vim - edit file 
- echo - print
